			description: [
				"When a Create machine stops, begin at the power source. Use goggles to verify rotation, follow every shaft and gearbox, then check the network's stress capacity and RPM."
				"A source can be spinning while the network is overstressed. Increasing speed may make the problem worse because many components consume more stress at higher RPM."
				"Test machines one operation at a time. A visible temporary shaft is better than a beautiful hidden network nobody can debug."
				"When a device is silent, trace rotation from the source one block at a time with Engineer's Goggles. Check reversed gearboxes, disconnected shafts, incorrect faces, overstress, and recipe requirements in that order."
