		{
			dependencies: ["5A53AAEC0E3B4B96"]
			description: [
				"The first Create engineers did not discover magic power. They learned to make ordinary rotation visible, measurable and reusable. Shafts became grammar; cogs became punctuation; factories became arguments built from motion."
				"Their best machines were understandable from a walkway. Their worst machines were sealed behind walls until one broken belt silenced an entire district."
				"Modern engineers honour them by building systems that can stop safely, explain themselves and serve more than one player's private ambition."
				"Write signs, books, map labels, and albums in plain practical language first. Lore becomes believable when another player can follow the road, reproduce the meal, repair the machine, or recognise the warning it preserves."
			]
			id: "71CEDD5D336CCB38"
